    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rolling In Gears is an engaging puzzle physics platformer game where you control a ball navigating through a series of mechanical challenges. The game\u2019s main mechanic revolves around rotating gears and moving platforms to guide the ball towards its target destination. Players need to carefully maneuver through the levels, using precision and timing to overcome obstacles and reach the end of each stage.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>How to Play Rolling in Gears</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Rolling in Gears, your goal is to guide a small ball through a series of intricate levels filled with mechanical obstacles and clever puzzles. Use the arrow keys to control the ball's movement, all with just two moves: forward and backward.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your challenge is to roll the ball forward and backward with precision as you navigate ramps, gears, and spinning hazards. Each level introduces new challenges, like gravity beams or suction mechanics, keeping you on your toes with emerging gameplay.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your timing and precision are key, especially when avoiding dangerous traps or timing your movements to perfection. The key is to watch out for platforms that shift or spin and think strategically to overcome trickier sections. If you get stuck, analyze the mechanics at play\u2014sometimes, it\u2019s about patience and letting the environment do the work for you; other times, it\u2019s all on you. There are 40 levels to master, each more difficult than the next.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rolling In Gears is an engaging puzzle physics platformer game where you control a ball navigating through a series of mechanical challenges. The game\u2019s main mechanic revolves around rotating gears and moving platforms to guide the ball towards its target destination. Players need to carefully maneuver through the levels, using precision and timing to overcome obstacles and reach the end of each stage.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>How to Play Rolling in Gears</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Rolling in Gears, your goal is to guide a small ball through a series of intricate levels filled with mechanical obstacles and clever puzzles. Use the arrow keys to control the ball's movement, all with just two moves: forward and backward.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your challenge is to roll the ball forward and backward with precision as you navigate ramps, gears, and spinning hazards. Each level introduces new challenges, like gravity beams or suction mechanics, keeping you on your toes with emerging gameplay.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your timing and precision are key, especially when avoiding dangerous traps or timing your movements to perfection. The key is to watch out for platforms that shift or spin and think strategically to overcome trickier sections. If you get stuck, analyze the mechanics at play\u2014sometimes, it\u2019s about patience and letting the environment do the work for you; other times, it\u2019s all on you. There are 40 levels to master, each more difficult than the next.</p>",
    "short_description": "Rolling In Gears is a physics-based puzzle platformer where you control everything except the player. Use precision and timing to manipulate shifting gears, ramps, and hazards across 40 levels. Master the mechanics, overcome obstacles, and reach the goal!",
